NEARS-3649 delta QA (fix cycle 2) — "Forgot your current password?" link renders
CENTERED, not right-aligned, contradicting the approved mockup (Jira comment
21169: "right-aligned directly under the Current Password field") and AC1 of
this delta QA task.

uiautomator dump (emulator-5554, EN locale) — the actual clickable Button node
for the link occupies the FULL row width, not a hugged/compact width:

  class=android.widget.Button bounds=[60,669][1284,801] width=1224
  (Current password field bounds=[60,525][1284,669] — same left/right edges
  as the link's row, confirming the link's clickable area spans the entire
  field width rather than hugging its label at the end.)

Root cause (packages/nears_dls/lib/components/npasswordformfields/n_password_form_fields.dart:153-162):

    if (current.forgotPasswordLabel != null)
      Align(
        alignment: AlignmentDirectional.centerEnd,
        child: NButton(
          text: current.forgotPasswordLabel!,
          variant: NVariant.tertiary,
          size: NSize.sm,
          onPressed: current.onForgotPassword,
        ),
      ),

`NButton.fullWidth` defaults to `true` (n_button.dart:118) and is NOT
overridden here. `NButton`'s tertiary-variant render (`_buildTertiary`,
n_button.dart:558-568) sizes its Container to `double.infinity` whenever
`fullWidth` is true, which fills the entire width offered by the outer
`Align` — nullifying `AlignmentDirectional.centerEnd` — and then internally
centers its label text (`Alignment.center`, n_button.dart:565). The result is
a full-width, visually CENTERED link instead of a right-aligned one.

The sibling "Need help? Contact Support" button in the SAME file (line
215-221) passes `fullWidth: false` explicitly and correctly hugs/right-hand-
positions its label — the "Forgot your current password?" call site is
missing that same flag.

Reproduces identically under Arabic/RTL (screenshot
delta-cp-forgot-link-ar.png) — the link is centered there too, confirming
this is a structural `fullWidth` defect, not a directionality-specific one.

Fix: add `fullWidth: false` to the NButton call at n_password_form_fields.dart:156-161
(matching the contactSupportLabel button's existing precedent).
